 "text": "Google built a button that changes how its AI shows your site to your readers.\n\nIt's called Google Preferred Sources, and it now runs inside AI Overviews and AI Mode.\n\nA reader clicks once. Google saves your whole domain as a source they prefer.\n\nFrom then on, when Google's AI cites your page, that reader sees a Preferred label on your link.\n\nNo ranking trick. The reader chose you, so Google's AI marks you.\n\nGoogle says people are twice as likely to click a preferred source. Over three hundred thousand sites are already picked.\n\nSetup takes two minutes: paste Google's script, or link to the preferences page with your domain.\n\nIt's live on our footer. Comment PREFERRED and I'll send the snippet.",
